      "answer_markdown": "Your bill went up by {F1}, from {F2} to {F3}. The main reasons were that the later period was colder, adding {F4} [E2][E1], the later bill covered more days, adding {F5} [E2][E1], and the earlier bill included a catch-up for an estimate that was too low, which had made it larger and so reduced the increase by {F6} [E2][E1][E4]. The unit rate went down, taking {F7} off the bill [E2][E1][E3], while the standing charge went up, adding {F8} [E2][E1][E3]. We also checked for credits, one-off charges, a fuel switch or usage changes beyond the weather, and none of those applied.",
